From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:13:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/27] llama/sycl : skip the causal KQ-mask upload, faster
 prefill uploads

Prefill at depth was dominated by host->device traffic: an f16 KQ mask
of n_tokens x n_kv is uploaded per ubatch for the target and again for
the MTP draft context. All switches default off:
- LLAMA_KQ_MASK_HINT=1|2|3: tag plain causal masks with their used
  length (2 = verify each tagged mask on the host, 3 = skip the upload;
  the device regenerates the mask when a kernel reads it)
- GGML_SYCL_FA_CAUSAL: prefill attention through oneDNN's implicit
  bottom-right causal mask when the tag is present
- GGML_SYCL_H2D_DIRECT: upload from pinned memory without the bounce copy
- GGML_SYCL_Q6K_DQ_FAST: faster q6_K reorder dequant (bit-identical)

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
